## Working hypothesis (to confirm or refute, not to assume)

The reset DID fire, but the CPU was halted (Break) when SWRSTREQ was
triggered. Per TC37x errata OCDS_TC.H018, the startup software restarts and
then re-halts on the retained DBGSR state before boot completes, so the
firmware never re-captured the stored reset-cause variable (RAM retains the
old value across a system reset — "unchanged stored value" cannot
distinguish no-reset from half-boot). The halted boot then feeds the newly
enabled recovery timers: RT0's alarm map includes GROUP7_ALARM30 (PFlash
FLASHCON configuration monitor — plausibly tripped by a boot strangled
mid-flash-configuration), a halted CPU cannot service the RT, and ~20 ms
later (RTD=1,000,000 at fBACK/2) it expires into ALM10[16] + FSP error-pin
activation (ALM10[18]) — killing CAN via the SBC and latching exactly AG7
and AG10. Related erratum OCDS_TC.H015 (spurious lockstep alarm, would show
in AG0) apparently did not fire — note if AG0 was clear.

## Tasks, in order — evidence first, target interaction last

1. HARVEST (no target interaction). From the failed run's evidence CSV and
   step notes, extract and report verbatim:
   - SCU_RSTSTAT_live (a set SW bit = the reset fired; 0x0 = either no reset
     or the half-boot got far enough to clear it)
   - stored rstStat and wStat (before and after rows)
   - all twelve AG words. Decode AG7 and AG10 bit by bit. Specifically:
     AG7 bit 30 (FLASHCON monitor, RT0-mapped), AG10 bit 16 (RT0 timeout),
     bit 17 (RT1 timeout), bit 18 (FSP error-pin activation), bit 22
     (access-enable error). State which hypothesis bits are present/absent.
2. SESSION-LOG CHECK (no target interaction). In the TRACE32/RCL log of the
   failed run: at the post-injection attach, was any core reported halted?
   Where was the PC (SSW/boot range vs application)? Any "stopped" or
   emulation-state messages. This is the H018 smoking gun.
3. LIVE READ (one non-intrusive attach: NoDebug then Attach, no Up/Down, no
   Go/Break). Read and record: SMU_RTC, SMU_RTAC00/01/10/11 (live RT
   mappings), SMU_STS (RTS0/1, RTME0/1), SMU_AG0..AG11, SCU_RSTSTAT,
   DBGSR of every CPU, and the TRACE32 settings SYStem.Option.DOWNMODE and
   SYStem.Option.EndInitProtectionOverride. Then NoDebug and detach.
4. CONTROLLED RE-TEST (only if 1-3 are captured and the DUT is in normal
   operation): repeat the system-reset injection with ONE change — after the
   RSTCON preselect/readback, issue Go and only then trigger
   SWRSTCON.SWRSTREQ as a runtime write (DUALPORT is ON), so no core is
   halted when the reset fires. Prediction if the hypothesis is right:
   stored cause updates to SYSTEM_RESET, AG7/AG10 stay clear, CAN stays up.
   Record the same evidence set either way.

## Safety rails

- Do NOT run the warm variant this slot.
- One non-resetting attach per step; if it fails, run the probe-health check
  and STOP — do not retry-storm, do not escalate to SYStem.Up or Down.
- Do not clear any latched alarm or reset-status register before it has been
  read and recorded.
- If anything deviates from the expected sequence, stop and report rather
  than improvising.
- Leave the DUT in Standby and the probe detached (NoDebug) at the end.

